# harness/conventions-terms - additional Korean transliterations that check [2] forbids.
#
# One term per line, `#` comments allowed. These ADD to the core set hard-coded in
# check-conventions.sh; they never replace it, so deleting or emptying this file cannot make
# the rule weaker than the core. A line carrying a regex metacharacter is ignored, so an entry
# is always a plain literal.
#
# The rule (docs/16 s3.1): a document is Korean prose whose IT and engineering terms stay in
# English. Write "server가 응답합니다", not "서버가 응답합니다".
#
# Why this file exists: measured against 85 transliterations a Korean rewrite actually
# produces, the core set caught 3. Add a term here the first time you catch yourself writing
# it, and add the pair to the docs/16 s3.1 table in the same change.

